  <h3>2. Data we collect</h3>
  <p>
    When you use the contact form, the quote request form or the interactive assistant, we
    collect the following information:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>First and last name</li>
    <li>Phone number</li>
    <li>Email address</li>
    <li>Date and venue of your wedding or event</li>
    <li>Your answers about your plans and the services you are interested in</li>
    <li>Any message you write</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When you request a free guide from the blog, we collect your first name, your email address,
    the guide requested and the page you came from.
  </p>

  <h3>3. Why we use your data</h3>
  <p>Your data is used only to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Answer your quote requests and questions</li>
    <li>Prepare a tailored quote for your event</li>
    <li>Follow up on your booking</li>
    <li>Email you the free guide you requested and, where relevant, get back in touch about your wedding</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>4. How long we keep it</h3>
  <p>
    Your data is kept for a maximum of 3 years from your last contact with us, and is then
    deleted.
  </p>

  <h3>5. Who receives your data</h3>
  <p>
    Your personal data is never sold, transferred or rented to third parties. Only Richard NIVET
    has access to it, for the purpose of managing his clients. Free guide requests are stored in
    a Google Sheets spreadsheet and the email is sent from a Gmail address: Google acts as a
    technical processor. To stop receiving emails, simply reply “stop” to the email you received.
  </p>

  <h3>6. Your rights</h3>
  <p>Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), you have the following rights:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Right of access: obtain a copy of your data</li>
    <li>Right to rectification: correct inaccurate data</li>
    <li>Right to erasure: ask for your data to be deleted</li>
    <li>Right to object: object to the processing of your data</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise these rights, email us at
    <ObfuscatedLink type="email" value="richarddjevent@gmail.com"><ObfuscatedText value="richarddjevent@gmail.com" /></ObfuscatedLink>.
  </p>

  <h3>7. Cookies</h3>
  <p>
    This website does not use any tracking or analytics cookies. Only strictly necessary technical
    cookies may be used for the site to work; they do not require consent. Visits are measured
    with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which sets no cookies, stores nothing in your browser and
    cannot identify you personally.
  </p>

  <h3>8. Security</h3>
  <p>
    We take all appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your data against
    unauthorised access, loss or disclosure.
  </p>

  <h3>9. Supervisory authority</h3>
  <p>
    If you believe your rights have not been respected, you can lodge a complaint with the CNIL,
    the French data protection authority:
    <a href="https://www.cnil.fr/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.cnil.fr</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
